WEBVTT

00:01.480 --> 00:03.470
A long, long time ago.

00:03.710 --> 00:06.080
About a hundred years ago.

00:06.550 --> 00:10.690
This? Why this is
the story of a little girl,

00:10.930 --> 00:13.360
who travelled beyond the Door of Destiny.

00:16.640 --> 00:17.440
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:18.000 --> 00:19.270
With your eyes

00:19.271 --> 00:20.539
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:21.753 --> 00:22.880
What do you see?

00:22.881 --> 00:24.010
Nani ga mieru

00:24.210 --> 00:25.650
Shining in the far distance,

00:25.651 --> 00:27.090
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.220 --> 00:28.325
The door to the future,

00:28.326 --> 00:29.430
Mirai no tobira

00:30.320 --> 00:31.940
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.941 --> 00:33.560
Sagashite iru

00:33.950 --> 00:37.515
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.660 --> 00:43.540
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:43.541 --> 00:45.420
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
- I'm sure there would be no more fighting
- Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.920 --> 00:50.525
It could be so much more fun

00:50.526 --> 00:52.130
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.210 --> 00:53.920
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:53.921 --> 00:55.630
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.050 --> 00:57.700
I can't see the end of the journey

00:57.701 --> 00:59.350
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
- God is the only one who could
possibly know - Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
- To the people who, someday, I will meet
again - Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.443 --> 01:07.500
I will go waving

01:07.501 --> 01:08.560
Te wo furinagara

01:08.860 --> 01:12.175
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:12.176 --> 01:15.489
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.490 --> 01:16.845
But I won't look back

01:16.846 --> 01:18.200
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.450 --> 01:20.930
Until the day my dream comes true

01:20.931 --> 01:23.410
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.660 --> 01:25.370
Nadja, Your smile

01:25.371 --> 01:27.079
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.080 --> 01:28.750
Nadja, gives me courage

01:28.751 --> 01:30.420
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.630 --> 01:32.090
Under the blue sky,

01:32.091 --> 01:33.549
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.550 --> 01:34.965
I will find the place

01:34.966 --> 01:36.380
Ashita no yukue

01:36.970 --> 01:38.785
where my future lies

01:38.786 --> 01:40.600
Mitsukeru kara

01:45.020 --> 01:50.060
London

02:05.400 --> 02:08.620
It's so easy to take money
away from commoners.

02:09.180 --> 02:12.660
They borrow money
without any knowledge then...

02:12.700 --> 02:15.280
they end up losing
everything to repay their debt.

02:15.840 --> 02:18.000
Geez, they're all such idiots.

02:34.420 --> 02:35.960
What an exquisite gem.

02:38.600 --> 02:40.780
In order to get this gem in your hands...

02:41.620 --> 02:44.050
How many people have you stepped on?

02:44.320 --> 02:45.840
You... It can't be...

02:46.460 --> 02:48.540
The noble flower that
blooms in the night...

02:50.140 --> 02:52.800
People call me the
phantom theif, Black Rose.

02:54.150 --> 02:55.960
The phantom thief. Black Rose...?

03:08.960 --> 03:11.520
Help, anybody! It's a thief!

03:17.840 --> 03:22.120
Night of the Phantom Theif, 'Black Rose'

03:23.960 --> 03:26.040
Master, what should we do about that girl?

03:26.260 --> 03:28.820
Yeah... I wonder...

03:30.240 --> 03:33.840
She's from the orphanage.
We can't just take her.

03:35.300 --> 03:36.336
You want to throw her out?

03:36.360 --> 03:39.300
But isn't she being chased by bad guys?

03:40.420 --> 03:41.820
Then why don't we take her with us?

03:41.940 --> 03:44.040
Would you think about
this seriously for a minute?

04:00.100 --> 04:02.300
You guys are... the guys from yesterday...

04:04.920 --> 04:05.920
What's wrong?

04:06.240 --> 04:07.260
What is this?!

04:07.580 --> 04:09.200
Hurry, get everyone outside!

04:13.520 --> 04:15.280
So, she has awoken, hasn't she...

04:17.280 --> 04:18.280
Good morning.

04:18.520 --> 04:19.520
Mornin'!

04:19.560 --> 04:20.880
Did you sleep well?

04:21.480 --> 04:23.340
Eh... Yes...

04:23.920 --> 04:25.660
Miss, what is your name?

04:26.060 --> 04:27.140
Umm...

04:27.680 --> 04:29.600
I don't know what's going on, but...

04:29.640 --> 04:31.060
Sorry to have been a bother.

04:31.420 --> 04:32.420
Goodbye!

04:32.600 --> 04:33.800
Ah, wait a sec!

04:43.100 --> 04:46.620
It's turning now, isn't it?
The wheels of Destiny...

04:49.540 --> 04:50.720
Everyone...

05:09.640 --> 05:11.560
The Applefield Orphanage...

05:12.520 --> 05:14.220
Our home is...

05:17.000 --> 05:18.120
Miss Appleton...

05:19.360 --> 05:20.940
Nadja is missing?

05:23.390 --> 05:24.390
Who are you?

05:24.700 --> 05:26.740
Hand over that brooch!

05:26.760 --> 05:28.600
Huh? This brooch?

05:29.340 --> 05:30.340
Why?!

05:31.460 --> 05:32.520
Those two...

05:34.400 --> 05:36.520
Do you have any idea where she may be?

05:36.840 --> 05:39.100
We're looking everywhere we can think of.

05:39.580 --> 05:41.200
The one they're after is...

05:41.240 --> 05:42.240
me?

05:42.440 --> 05:43.440
Miss Appleton!

05:44.200 --> 05:45.200
Nadja is...?

05:45.260 --> 05:46.260
nowhere to be seen.

05:46.360 --> 05:49.020
What if... she's dead?

05:50.520 --> 05:52.180
Nadja is definitely alive!

05:52.340 --> 05:53.340
Definitely...

05:53.560 --> 05:55.740
She's probably just
playing hide-and-seek...

05:55.920 --> 05:58.280
But, I'll definitely find her!

05:58.660 --> 05:59.660
Oliver...

05:59.760 --> 06:01.160
You must get ready.

06:01.220 --> 06:03.780
They'll be here to take you
to your apprenticeship soon.

06:04.100 --> 06:05.660
I still have time!

06:05.820 --> 06:07.760
Until the last moment, I'll...

06:08.600 --> 06:11.460
We haven't looked in the western woods yet.

06:11.560 --> 06:12.560
Yeah!

06:13.040 --> 06:14.440
Wait for us!

06:19.980 --> 06:20.980
Everyone...

06:21.440 --> 06:24.980
As soon as Nadja turns
up, please let us know.

06:25.420 --> 06:26.660
I understand.

06:32.420 --> 06:34.960
She must have gotten away
in the confusion of the fire.

06:35.020 --> 06:37.380
That's because you dropped the lamp.

06:37.400 --> 06:39.120
You're the one who dropped it!

06:40.040 --> 06:42.380
Damn! If that guy hadn't
interfered at that moment...

06:46.680 --> 06:49.840
that brooch would
have been in our hands!

06:50.000 --> 06:52.060
Damn it!

06:53.600 --> 06:55.400
Because they were after me...

06:55.860 --> 06:56.900
The orphanage was...

07:01.740 --> 07:05.300
If I stay... I'll certainly... bring
trouble to everyone...

07:06.160 --> 07:07.660
Oliver, take care.

07:07.900 --> 07:09.000
Do your best.

07:09.260 --> 07:10.260
Yeah!

07:10.980 --> 07:11.700
Alex...

07:11.980 --> 07:12.980
I understand.

07:13.200 --> 07:15.420
We will definitely find Nadja.

07:15.900 --> 07:16.900
I'm leaving it up to you.

07:20.620 --> 07:23.700
I'm sorry, Oliver...
This is for the best.

07:34.120 --> 07:36.140
Goodbye, everyone.

07:37.260 --> 07:39.420
Goodbye, Applefield.

07:43.080 --> 07:44.120
Geez...

07:44.460 --> 07:46.660
I wonder what happened to that girl...

07:46.980 --> 07:48.760
Granny, what are you making?

07:49.300 --> 07:52.060
A ballet dancer's tutu.

07:52.320 --> 07:54.700
A tutu? For who?

07:54.720 --> 07:56.460
Heh, it's a secret.

07:56.960 --> 07:57.960
Huh?

07:58.920 --> 08:00.200
"Dear Miss Appleton,"

08:00.660 --> 08:02.540
"I'm sorry for having you worried."

08:02.560 --> 08:04.020
"I am quite all right."

08:04.760 --> 08:09.840
"It was the happiest time to be with you,
all. Just like a real family in Applefield."

08:10.360 --> 08:14.220
"Thank you so much for everything."

08:14.280 --> 08:17.100
"Lots of love, Nadja."

08:18.580 --> 08:21.340
Miss Appleton...
Where did Nadja go?

08:23.320 --> 08:24.560
Miss Appleton...

08:34.240 --> 08:36.300
Nadja...!!!

08:36.760 --> 08:38.920
Nadja...!

08:45.300 --> 08:47.180
What should I do from here...?

08:50.280 --> 08:54.050
I didn't know there was a ring inside...

08:55.400 --> 08:56.420
Mother.

08:57.840 --> 09:01.500
This ring... did Mother
ever wear this ring?

09:01.760 --> 09:02.760
Ah?

09:03.120 --> 09:06.100
That brooch that you were wearing
when you were handed to me,

09:06.940 --> 09:10.120
is an important thing that
ties you and your mother.

09:14.720 --> 09:15.720
Mother...

09:16.280 --> 09:18.060
Mother...!

09:21.360 --> 09:24.000
Mother, you're alive somewhere.

09:24.780 --> 09:27.280
I'm going to find you, Mother!

09:27.400 --> 09:28.260
For sure!

09:28.280 --> 09:30.840
So please... Wait for me!

09:36.020 --> 09:38.000
Please let me work here.

09:38.440 --> 09:42.080
I'll be 13 years old soon.
I can work just as hard as anyone else.

09:42.420 --> 09:44.520
I'm afraid, I've already
got enough workers.

09:45.860 --> 09:48.180
In England at this time...

09:48.900 --> 09:52.580
It was normal for all children,
except the children of the wealthy...

09:52.760 --> 09:56.780
to take a job at around the age of 13.

10:00.940 --> 10:03.360
The world can be so harsh...

10:04.280 --> 10:05.620
I'm so hungry...

10:08.060 --> 10:08.780
Geez!

10:08.840 --> 10:10.380
It's Mr. Black Rose.

10:11.540 --> 10:14.980
"Last night, he appeared in the
mansion of a loan shark," it says.

10:15.400 --> 10:19.100
If the Black Rose was after
him, he must be pretty bad.

10:20.860 --> 10:21.960
Like always,

10:22.020 --> 10:26.030
everything he stole was
divided amongst the poor.

10:26.060 --> 10:27.780
Black Rose is on our side.

10:28.600 --> 10:31.020
He must be a lovely person.

10:31.620 --> 10:33.100
A phantom thief, huh?

10:33.700 --> 10:35.800
If I don't find work soon,

10:35.940 --> 10:38.040
I might have to become a thief as well...

10:39.620 --> 10:42.460
Idiot, idiot! What are
you thinking, Nadja?!

10:47.840 --> 10:48.980
This music...

11:03.620 --> 11:04.880
There's no mistake about it.

11:06.340 --> 11:07.340
But...

11:07.420 --> 11:11.060
Even after they saved me, I
ran off barely saying thank you.

11:11.320 --> 11:13.680
How can I go back now...?

11:14.760 --> 11:15.760
But...

11:17.360 --> 11:19.540
- Excuse me.
- Huh?

11:20.020 --> 11:22.060
Please let me join the troupe!

11:49.720 --> 11:50.720
Please!

11:51.060 --> 11:52.680
Please let me join the troupe!

11:54.560 --> 11:55.960
How presumptuous of you.

11:57.620 --> 12:00.060
You're the one who ran off
without even telling us your name.

12:00.380 --> 12:03.520
It's Nadja.
I'm Nadja Applefield.

12:03.960 --> 12:05.660
That's not what I meant.

12:05.940 --> 12:07.880
So, what can you do?

12:08.140 --> 12:08.520
Eh?

12:08.840 --> 12:09.840
Huh?

12:10.260 --> 12:14.920
The Dandelion Troupe can't afford
to take on someone who's useless.

12:15.420 --> 12:16.980
Do you have anything you can do?

12:17.260 --> 12:19.100
Yes! I can dance!

12:19.520 --> 12:20.700
Dance, huh?

12:21.460 --> 12:23.200
Well, can you show us?

12:23.660 --> 12:24.660
Yes!

12:25.100 --> 12:28.200
Ooh! It suits you very well!

12:28.240 --> 12:29.920
Go ahead, put that on and dance.

12:30.080 --> 12:31.640
Eh? Is it it okay?

12:31.680 --> 12:35.020
Of course! I made it just for you!

12:35.060 --> 12:36.740
It's even the exact size.

12:37.860 --> 12:40.560
Silvie. Please do her hair up.

12:42.500 --> 12:44.180
If you say so, Granny.

12:44.600 --> 12:45.600
Come with me.

12:46.100 --> 12:47.100
Yes!

13:02.620 --> 13:04.200
Thank you for waiting!

13:13.940 --> 13:15.420
Thomas, that "thing".

13:21.200 --> 13:22.200
What is this?

13:22.380 --> 13:23.700
O-open it, please?

13:24.000 --> 13:25.000
Okay.

13:39.600 --> 13:41.760
Y-You have to hold
that... while you dance...

13:43.020 --> 13:44.740
Now, I'll start the music.

13:45.000 --> 13:47.980
-Well, relax and do your best
- Umm... the choreography?

13:48.280 --> 13:51.060
Anyone can imitate
someone else's choreography.

13:51.400 --> 13:52.640
If you wish to join us,

13:52.760 --> 13:55.460
you'll have to be a dancer who
can come up with her own dance.

13:56.080 --> 13:57.520
Come up with a dance?

14:06.080 --> 14:08.260
Master, you sure a meanie.

14:08.680 --> 14:10.660
You want her to give
up on her own, don't you?

14:11.180 --> 14:12.180
I wonder...

14:29.640 --> 14:31.600
Eh? Not bad, not bad.

15:10.160 --> 15:13.000
Whether she's worthy to
become a member or not...

15:13.100 --> 15:15.260
Well, I guess the applause answers that.

15:17.540 --> 15:20.380
The Dandelion Troupe's glorious dancer...

15:21.160 --> 15:22.640
Lady Nadja!

15:23.540 --> 15:25.570
Bravo!

15:31.660 --> 15:35.180
I'm the master of the
Dandelion Troupe, George.

15:35.500 --> 15:37.080
And this is Granny.

15:39.980 --> 15:41.160
I'm Silvie.

15:41.360 --> 15:43.520
Nadja, let me ask you something.

15:43.960 --> 15:47.160
We're travelling entertainers
who travel from place to place.

15:47.600 --> 15:50.339
We don't know when we
can come back to this city.

15:50.340 --> 15:51.920
Are you okay with that?

15:52.580 --> 15:55.740
I... can't return to the orphanage anymore.

15:56.100 --> 15:58.200
I'm sure you have your reasons.

15:59.760 --> 16:01.520
I'm the pierrot, Abel.

16:02.140 --> 16:04.300
This is the guy in charge
of instruments, Thomas.

16:04.480 --> 16:05.840
H-hello.

16:06.160 --> 16:07.160
Nice to meet you.

16:10.800 --> 16:12.240
This girl here is Rita.

16:15.380 --> 16:19.200
She's saying, "These lions
are Crème and Chocolat."

16:19.480 --> 16:20.840
Rita can't speak...

16:24.820 --> 16:26.040
Rita, how old are you?

16:27.820 --> 16:29.500
I see, you're 5 years old.

16:30.980 --> 16:32.520
I'll be 13 years old soon.

16:32.540 --> 16:34.310
Nice to meet you.

16:37.220 --> 16:38.640
All right! Let's head off!

16:39.500 --> 16:40.960
Where are we going?

16:41.000 --> 16:44.219
To the biggest city in
all of England. London!

16:44.220 --> 16:45.799
London

16:45.800 --> 16:49.200
Sorry to have kept you waiting Lord Herman.

16:49.600 --> 16:51.640
Right now, we sent a
message to the Duke in Vienna.

16:52.540 --> 16:53.960
What did Father say?

16:54.380 --> 16:58.400
He's ordered us to find his
granddaughter, Nadja, as soon as possible.

16:58.640 --> 17:03.180
We haven't found her yet. And,
there are zero clues... or so we told him.

17:05.140 --> 17:06.540
That stubborn old man.

17:06.860 --> 17:09.840
He doesn't even stop to be
concerned about me, his son.

17:12.080 --> 17:15.440
That girl "Nadja"...
Just who exactly is she?

17:16.040 --> 17:18.160
She's my older sister's daughter.

17:19.180 --> 17:22.480
Then that means, she's
your niece, Lord Herman?

17:23.120 --> 17:26.120
The ring in that brooch that girl has...

17:26.560 --> 17:31.440
is proof that she's a member
of the ducal Preminger family.

17:31.720 --> 17:36.360
She has the right to inherit
the dukedom and the fortune.

17:36.840 --> 17:38.600
But... By the order of succession...

17:38.640 --> 17:41.500
Lord Herman who is the son of the duke...

17:41.560 --> 17:43.400
should inherit the dukedom.

17:43.880 --> 17:45.200
But Father...

17:45.560 --> 17:49.000
intends for the girl to inherit
the dukedom, instead of me.

17:50.560 --> 17:54.580
My... Lord Herman, the
duke must really hate you.

17:57.100 --> 17:58.420
Please excuse us.

17:58.860 --> 18:02.400
I will be the one to inherit
the Preminger dukedom!

18:02.560 --> 18:06.600
But, Lord Herman, this
job is a lot of hard work.

18:07.820 --> 18:08.820
Right?

18:08.940 --> 18:10.400
We need something in advance...

18:13.200 --> 18:15.080
I don't care how you do it.

18:15.580 --> 18:18.800
Just get that girl's brooch and ring.

18:18.880 --> 18:19.880
Understand?

18:19.920 --> 18:20.920
Yes!

18:35.100 --> 18:40.990
London in those days had a
well-developed transportation system...

18:41.000 --> 18:43.880
And was a large metropolis with
a population of about 6.5 million.

18:46.020 --> 18:48.680
Awesome! Awesome, awesome!

18:48.740 --> 18:49.880
So this is London!

18:49.920 --> 18:51.560
Is this your first time in London?

18:51.760 --> 18:52.760
Yes!

18:54.780 --> 18:57.960
All right, tonight we hold a
welcoming party for Nadja!

18:58.120 --> 19:00.779
Abel, go buy some wine, and a lot of it!

19:00.780 --> 19:03.560
No can do. You have to
moderate your drinking.

19:03.680 --> 19:05.220
Gee, you're such a nag!

19:05.260 --> 19:06.620
It's for Nadja.

19:06.720 --> 19:09.660
You say that, but you just want to drink.

19:42.700 --> 19:44.740
You guys couldn't sleep either?

19:56.660 --> 19:58.900
I wonder how everyone's doing...

20:02.360 --> 20:05.280
Ah! Crème, Chocolat! Come back, please!

20:05.680 --> 20:07.240
You'll get lost!

20:13.560 --> 20:15.080
Ahh, shall we go back?

20:16.900 --> 20:18.500
Where... am I?

20:25.820 --> 20:27.480
I got lost...

20:34.920 --> 20:37.360
What do I do?

21:08.500 --> 21:10.160
Where are you, Black Rose?

21:10.200 --> 21:11.200
Black Rose?!

21:11.960 --> 21:13.020
The phantom theif?

21:22.040 --> 21:25.040
What? What? This guy is a thief, right?

21:26.180 --> 21:29.220
But those people a while ago
said he's on the side of the people...

21:29.640 --> 21:31.900
but this is not the time
to think about such things!

21:32.520 --> 21:33.520
Where are you?!

21:33.620 --> 21:35.100
You won't get away!

21:36.080 --> 21:38.620
You're so thin, skinny girl.

21:39.780 --> 21:41.940
That's so rude! Why did
you say that all of a sudden?

21:42.400 --> 21:44.320
There are many evil
people in the city at night.

21:44.760 --> 21:46.640
A child shouldn't be
wandering around at night.

21:53.200 --> 21:56.200
What the heck?! I'm not a child!

21:56.540 --> 21:58.260
I'll be 13 years old soon!

21:58.560 --> 22:01.920
What's more, a thief
has no right to tell me that!

22:02.440 --> 22:04.020
Idiot!!!

22:14.490 --> 22:16.115
Paris is sunnier than London

22:16.116 --> 22:17.740
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.370 --> 22:24.455
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:24.456 --> 22:27.540
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
- Indeed
- Kitto

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
- It's not use worrying about it
- Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:35.500 --> 22:37.065
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:37.066 --> 22:38.630
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.890 --> 22:41.245
Tomorrow's going to
be whatever it was meant

22:41.246 --> 22:43.600
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
- To be, to be
- Naru naru

22:45.390 --> 22:47.895
The tree fog won

22:47.896 --> 22:50.400
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.860 --> 22:52.820
The world frog-jumping contest

22:52.821 --> 22:54.780
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.990 --> 23:01.075
Under the kitten's paw

23:01.076 --> 23:04.160
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:04.580 --> 23:07.665
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:07.666 --> 23:10.750
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:13.590 --> 23:15.255
Paris is sunnier than London

23:15.256 --> 23:16.920
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:20.510 --> 23:23.700
It's not the time to hang around

23:23.701 --> 23:26.890
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:27.770 --> 23:30.020
Indeed, indeed

23:30.021 --> 23:32.270
Kitto kitto

23:40.530 --> 23:41.730
- Tomorrow's Nadja
- Tomorrow's Nadja

23:43.110 --> 23:45.110
The mechanical automobile got stolen.

23:45.530 --> 23:48.830
With Rita on board, it started
to run at an incredible speed.

23:49.880 --> 23:51.820
It ran over stores, one after another...

23:52.120 --> 23:54.060
causing a big panic
in the city of London!

23:54.580 --> 23:56.950
Please? Someone stop that car!

23:57.750 --> 24:01.540
Eh? It's a Japanese boy who's driving it?

24:02.640 --> 24:03.820
<i>Tomorrow's Nadja:</i>

24:03.940 --> 24:05.800
Samurai Kennosuke's Wild Ride!!

24:07.321 --> 24:08.870
Now the Door of Destiny opens.
